{"name":"Undercut / fade with textured top","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Paul_De_La_Cruz_pauldlc_undercut_hair_style.PNG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_De_La_Cruz_pauldlc_undercut_hair_style.PNG","caption":"Paul De La Cruz pauldlc undercut hair style","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":2,"casual":{"lead":["A short faded side and back with a longer, textured top gives a clean outline and volume on top, and a skin fade is said to make the face and jaw look sharper.","The undercut dates to early 20th-century working-class men, was mainstream in the 1920s and 1930s and revived in the early 2010s, with adopters such as David Beckham. It is frequently cited in men's grooming advice as a flattering cut for many face shapes; those claims come from stylists and forums, not studies."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People ask a barber for a fade or tapered sides and keep length on top, then style it with matte clay or paste for texture. It needs a trim every few weeks to keep the fade sharp, and the new look shows straight away."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Low risk. Maintenance is frequent, and the look needs enough hair on top to style."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Paul_De_La_Cruz_pauldlc_undercut_hair_style.PNG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Paul_De_La_Cruz_pauldlc_undercut_hair_style.PNG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Paul De La Cruz pauldlc undercut hair style","license":"CC0","creator":"Pmjn","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_De_La_Cruz_pauldlc_undercut_hair_style.PNG","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wi